1 0 0 1 50 497.89 Tm (#### Destructible Obstacle Rules & Energy Constraints) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 483.89 Tm (1. Robot starts with $10$ energy units.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 469.89 Tm (2. The robot cannot step directly onto an intact blue cell; it must **destroy** the) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 455.89 Tm (obstacle from an adjacent accessible cell prior to entry.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 441.89 Tm (3. Destroying any blue cell consumes **2 energy units** and incurs a **navigation) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 427.89 Tm (cost of +5 units**.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 413.89 Tm (4. Once destroyed, a blue obstacle permanently becomes an ordinary free cell and) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 399.89 Tm (remains accessible for all subsequent movements.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 385.89 Tm (5. **Bonus cells \($B+$\):** Entering a bonus cell awards $+3$ energy units upon first) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 371.89 Tm (entry.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 357.89 Tm (6. **Penalty cells \($B-$\):** Entering a penalty cell incurs an additional navigation) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 343.89 Tm (cost of $+5$ units upon first entry.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 329.89 Tm (7. Energy can never become negative; if remaining energy $< 2$, destruction cannot) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 315.89 Tm (occur, rendering that intact blue cell impassable.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 301.89 Tm (8. Each bonus or penalty effect applies **exactly once** per cell.) Tj
