1 0 0 1 50 777.89 Tm (#### 2. Identification of Vertices, Edges, and Movement Costs) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 763.89 Tm (* **Vertices:** Each vertex is a state tuple $s = \(x, y, \\text{energy},) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 749.89 Tm (\\text{mask}\)$.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 735.89 Tm (* **Edges:** A directed edge exists from state $s$ to state $s'$ if:) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 721.89 Tm (  1. $\(x', y'\)$ is within grid boundaries \($1 \\le x', y' \\le 15$\).) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 707.89 Tm (  2. $\(x', y'\)$ is not a permanent orange obstacle \($O$\).) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 693.89 Tm (  3. If $\(x', y'\)$ is an intact blue cell, the robot has energy $\\ge 2$ to destroy) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 679.89 Tm (it.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 665.89 Tm (* **Costs:** ) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 651.89 Tm (  $$\\text{Edge Cost} = \\text{Movement Cost} + \(\\text{Destruction Cost if intact: } 5\)) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 637.89 Tm (+ \(\\text{Penalty Cost if } B-: 5\)$$) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 623.89 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 50 609.89 Tm (#### 3. Representation of Permanent and Destructible Obstacles) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 595.89 Tm (* **Permanent Obstacles \($O$\):** Excluded entirely from the vertex set. No directed) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 581.89 Tm (edge enters an orange cell.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 567.89 Tm (* **Destructible Obstacles \($B, B+, B-$\):** Maintained via an indexed bitmask. An) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 553.89 Tm (intact blue cell acts as a conditional barrier requiring an energy threshold of $2$.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 539.89 Tm (Once destroyed, its bit is set to $1$ in the bitmask, and it acts as an ordinary free) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 525.89 Tm (cell carrying standard movement costs with no further energy deduction or) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 511.89 Tm (bonus/penalty re-triggering.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 497.89 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 50 483.89 Tm (#### 4. How the Graph Evolves Upon Destruction) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 469.89 Tm (Graph evolution is captured without mutating the underlying grid array by) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 455.89 Tm (transitioning between **state-space layers**. The bitmask has $15$ bits \(one per blue) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 441.89 Tm (cell\). Destruction transitions the robot from a state in layer $\\text{mask}$ to a) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 427.89 Tm (state in layer $\\text{mask} \\mid \(1 \\ll i\)$. In this new layer, cell $i$ has incoming) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 413.89 Tm (edges from all adjacent accessible cells with normal step costs, reflecting permanent) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 399.89 Tm (accessibility.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 385.89 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 50 371.89 Tm (#### 5. Directed vs. Undirected Nature of the Graph) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 357.89 Tm (The navigation graph is strictly **DIRECTED** for three fundamental reasons:) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 343.89 Tm (1. **Asymmetry of Movement Costs:** Reversing a move has an asymmetric cost. Moving) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 329.89 Tm (Right has cost $+2$, but moving Left has cost $-1$. Moving Up has cost $+2$, but) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 315.89 Tm (moving Down has cost $-1$. Moving Up-Right has cost $+3$, but its reverse is not even) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 301.89 Tm (an allowed movement.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 287.89 Tm (2. **Asymmetry of Movement Directions:** Permitted directions are $\\{R, L, U, D, UR,) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 273.89 Tm (UL\\}$. Downward diagonal transitions \($DR, DL$\) do not exist. Therefore, an edge $\(x,) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 259.89 Tm (y\) \\rightarrow \(x+1, y+1\)$ via $UR$ has no reciprocal edge $\(x+1, y+1\) \\rightarrow) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 245.89 Tm (\(x, y\)$.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 231.89 Tm (3. **One-Way State Transitions:** Destroying an obstacle consumes energy and) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 217.89 Tm (permanently alters the bitmask. This is an irreversible, strictly one-way state) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 203.89 Tm (transition.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 189.89 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 50 175.89 Tm (#### 6. Robot State Definition) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 161.89 Tm (A state is formally defined as:) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 147.89 Tm ($$s = \(x, y, \\text{energy}, \\text{mask}\)$$) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 133.89 Tm (Where:) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 119.88999999999999 Tm (* $x \\in \\{1, \\dots, 15\\}$: Column coordinate.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 105.88999999999999 Tm (* $y \\in \\{1, \\dots, 15\\}$: Row coordinate.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 91.88999999999999 Tm (* $\\text{energy} \\in \\{0, \\dots, 10\\}$: Current remaining energy units.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 77.88999999999999 Tm (* $\\text{mask} \\in \\{0, \\dots, 2^{15}-1\\}$: An integer bitmask where bit $i = 1$) Tj
