1 0 0 1 50 511.89 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 50 497.89 Tm (#### Discussion: Does BFS Guarantee a Minimum-Cost Path?) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 483.89 Tm (**Answer: NO.** BFS guarantees the shortest path **only in terms of edge count) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 469.89 Tm (\(unweighted fewest hops\)**, or when all edge weights are identical and positive.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 455.89 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 50 441.89 Tm (In this environment, BFS does not guarantee a minimum-cost path because:) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 427.89 Tm (1. **Asymmetric & Negative Edge Costs:** Edge costs vary from $-3$ to $+3$. A path) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 413.89 Tm (with fewer hops can accumulate expensive positive edges, whereas a longer path) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 399.89 Tm (utilizing negative edges \(Left $-1$, Down $-1$, Up-Left $-3$\) can achieve a lower) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 385.89 Tm (total cost.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 371.89 Tm (2. **Negative-Cost Cycles:** The graph contains directed cycles with negative net) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 357.89 Tm (cost:) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 343.89 Tm (   $$\\text{Up-Left } \(-3\) + \\text{Right } \(+2\) + \\text{Down } \(-1\) = -2$$) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 329.89 Tm (   Traversing this 3-cell loop returns the robot to the starting coordinate with a) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 315.89 Tm (net cost reduction of $-2$. Because BFS ignores costs during frontier expansion, it) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 301.89 Tm (fails to exploit cost-reducing transitions.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 287.89 Tm (3. **Empirical Proof:** BFS found a 15-move path costing **51**. However, our DFS) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 273.89 Tm (experiment with reverse successor ordering discovered a 78-move path costing only) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 259.89 Tm (**34**. This conclusively proves that BFS does not minimize cost in this setting.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 245.89 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 50 231.89 Tm (---) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 217.89 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 50 203.89 Tm (### 1.4 Task 3: Depth-First Search \(DFS\) Navigation) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 189.89 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 50 175.89 Tm (Two DFS implementations were developed:) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 161.89 Tm (* **\(a\) Iterative DFS:** Implemented with an explicit custom LIFO Stack. To ensure) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 147.89 Tm (strict equivalence with recursive DFS, successor states are pushed in **reverse) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 133.89 Tm (order** so that the first successor is popped and explored first. Marking occurs upon) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 119.88999999999999 Tm (pop.) Tj
