1 0 0 1 50 791.89 Tm (   * Most critically, the directed graph contains **negative-cost cycles**:) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 777.89 Tm (     $$\\text{Up-Left } \(-3\) + \\text{Right } \(+2\) + \\text{Down } \(-1\) = -2$$) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 763.89 Tm (   * In a graph with negative cycles, a minimum-cost walk is **unbounded below) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 749.89 Tm (\($-\\infty$\)** because traversing the loop repeatedly reduces total cost indefinitely.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 735.89 Tm (For simple paths \(no repeated vertices\), the problem is NP-hard. BFS does not) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 721.89 Tm (evaluate edge weights and thus cannot minimize cost.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 707.89 Tm () Tj
